POI Monitor
===========

Lightweight sentinel system for detecting changes in Google Maps POI data.
Periodically scans 4 key fields (reviewCount, rating, openingHours, popularTimes),
identifies changed POIs, and outputs place_id lists for targeted re-scraping by
the upstream batch scraper system.


Prerequisites
-------------

- Node.js >= 18
- Chromium (installed via Playwright)

    npm install
    npx playwright install chromium


Quick Start
-----------

    # Import baseline data
    node cli.js import --source /path/to/scraper/output

    # Run a test scan (50 POIs)
    node cli.js scan --limit 50

    # View database stats
    node cli.js stats

    # Or use the interactive menu
    bash monitor.sh


Architecture
------------

                 +-----------------+
                 |   cli.js        |  CLI entry (commander)
                 +--------+--------+
                          |
          +---------------+---------------+
          |               |               |
  +-------v------+ +-----v------+ +------v-------+
  | baseline-    | | change-    | | poi-         |
  | importer.js  | | scanner.js | | discovery.js |
  +--------------+ +-----+------+ +--------------+
          |               |               |
          |        +------v------+        |
          |        | extract-poi-|        |
          |        | data.js     |        |
          |        +-------------+        |
          |               |               |
  +-------v---------------v---------------v--+
  |              db.js (SQLite)               |
  +-------------------------------------------+


Commands
--------

import    Import baseline data from scraper output.

          node cli.js import --source <path> [--format auto|old|new]

          Supported formats:
            old - Directory tree: {Category}/{PlaceId}/rev_data/reviews.json
            new - NDJSON files with business, openingHours, popularTimes fields

scan      Run change detection scan against baseline.

          node cli.js scan [--limit <n>] [--resume]

          Launches Playwright browsers, navigates to each POI page,
          extracts current data, compares with baseline, and records changes.
          Generates a report and snapshot on completion.

stats     Display database statistics.

          node cli.js stats

report    View or regenerate a scan report.

          node cli.js report --scan-id <id>

discover  Discover new POIs by geographic sampling and Google Maps search.

          node cli.js discover [--city <name>] [--categories <list>]
                               [--cell-size <meters>] [--points <n>]
                               [--boundary <file>] [--limit <n>]

          Generates sampling points within city boundary using Lloyd
          relaxation, then searches Google Maps at each point for POIs
          not yet in the database.

clean-scan
          Clean a bad scan and restore corrupted baseline values.

          node cli.js clean-scan --scan-id <id>


Monitored Fields
----------------

Field             Comparison Method    Notes
-----             -----------------    -----
reviewCount       Exact integer        null->value not reported as change
rating            Float tolerance 0.05 null->value not reported as change
openingHoursHash  Exact string (SHA256) Normalized before hashing
popularTimesHash  Exact string (SHA256) Normalized before hashing


Change Types
------------

REVIEW_CHANGE         reviewCount or rating changed
HOURS_CHANGE          openingHours changed
POPULAR_TIMES_CHANGE  popularTimes changed
MULTI_CHANGE          Both review fields and hours/times changed
POI_GONE              POI page failed to load N consecutive times
NEW_POI               POI found via discovery that is not in database


Database Schema
---------------

poi_baseline
  placeId            TEXT PRIMARY KEY
  name               TEXT
  reviewCount        INTEGER
  rating             REAL
  openingHoursHash   TEXT
  popularTimesHash   TEXT
  navigablePlaceId   TEXT        ChIJ format ID for URL navigation
  lastCheckedAt      TEXT
  consecutiveFailures INTEGER   Default 0
  status             TEXT        active | gone
  sourceFormat       TEXT        old | new | discovered
  importedAt         TEXT
  updatedAt          TEXT

change_log
  id                 INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
  scanId             TEXT
  placeId            TEXT
  changeType         TEXT
  fields             TEXT (JSON)
  detectedAt         TEXT

scan_history
  scanId             TEXT PRIMARY KEY
  startedAt          TEXT
  completedAt        TEXT
  totalPois          INTEGER
  scannedCount       INTEGER
  changedCount       INTEGER
  failedCount        INTEGER
  summary            TEXT (JSON)
  status             TEXT


Output Structure
----------------

output/
  reports/
    YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM/
      change_report.json      Full change details with URLs
      changed_placeids.txt    One place_id per line (scraper input)
  snapshots/
    baseline_YYYY-MM-DD.json  Full database export
  discovery/
    {city}_boundary.geojson   Cached city boundary


Configuration
-------------

config/monitor-config.json

  concurrency.browsers          Number of browser instances (default: 3)
  concurrency.tabsPerBrowser    Tabs per browser (default: 5)
  thresholds.ratingTolerance    Float comparison tolerance (default: 0.05)
  thresholds.consecutiveFailuresForGone
                                Failures before marking POI gone (default: 5)
  thresholds.poiTimeoutMs       Per-POI timeout in ms (default: 10000)
  thresholds.navigationTimeoutMs Navigation timeout in ms (default: 30000)
  scan.batchSize                POIs per batch (default: 100)
  scan.delayBetweenBatchesMs    Delay between batches (default: 1000)
  browser.headless              Run headless (default: true)


Data Extraction Strategy
------------------------

The scanner uses a two-step page loading approach:

  1. Load search API URL to initialize Google Maps session
  2. Load place URL for full APP_INITIALIZATION_STATE data

Data extraction priority:

  rating       DOM first ([role="img"][aria-label*="star"]), APP_STATE fallback
  reviewCount  DOM first (button text / aria-label), APP_STATE fallback
  openingHours APP_STATE only (not available in DOM)
  popularTimes APP_STATE only (not available in DOM)

Page load verification uses placeId presence in URL/APP_STATE rather than
DOM element checks, which avoids false failures from SPA rendering delays.


PlaceId Formats
---------------

Two formats coexist in the database:

  Old (ChIJ):  ChIJOW9NG7QP2jEROd_IfYBoP-s    Works in place_id: URLs
  New (hex):   0x31da0fb41b4d6f39:0xeb3f...     Does NOT work in place_id: URLs

The navigablePlaceId column stores the ChIJ format extracted from NDJSON _meta
for hex-format POIs, ensuring correct URL navigation in reports and scanning.


